  source.js
      imports parseUnifiedDiff / hunkLineCounts / hunkNewSpan from
      ../code-review/source.js and delegates enumeration to it.
      <- open-code-review internal/diff/hunk.go (hunkHeaderRe) and
         internal/diff/parser.go, via domains/code-review/source.js.
      Deviation: none in the reused parser. This domain adds the `bundleReport`
      join onto `candidate.meta.chunkBytes`; it does not change which candidates
      exist, their ids, their locators or the gate predicates that see them.

  anchor.js
      re-exports ../code-review/anchor.js unchanged (object identity; the
      domain's test asserts `anchor === codeReviewAnchor`).
      <- open-code-review internal/diff/resolver.go. The same deviation
         documented in the root NOTICE for domains/code-review/anchor.js
         applies verbatim: upstream's third tier re-locates with a model call;
         this port stops at "unanchored" and distinguishes `locator-mismatch`
         from `relocation-ambiguous`.
      Known limitation carried over from the reference implementation: the
      normaliser strips a LEADING `+` or `-` from both the excerpt and the
      document line, so a legitimate whole-line quote that itself begins with
      `-` (a CSS custom property such as `--focus-ring: …`, a YAML list item, a
      `--flag`) is refused as a no-match. The fixtures avoid such lines and the
      limitation is reported rather than papered over; a local "fix" here would
      make this domain's anchor tolerance differ from the reference, which is
      exactly what the reuse rule forbids.

  evidence.js
      spreads ../code-review/evidence.js's three tools into its toolkit by
      function identity, and adds `render_scope`.
      <- the layout of internal/tool/file_read.go and internal/tool/git_grep.go
         (bounded read/search payloads) via domains/code-review/evidence.js.
      `render_scope` is ORIGINAL to this project: a bounded, pattern-based walk
      from a line up to the enclosing component/scope. It reports UNKNOWN when
      it finds no scope opener instead of guessing, and its `provenance` says it
      is not a parser.

  index.js
      gate.extensions
      <- internal/config/allowlist/supported_file_types.json via
         domains/code-review/index.js. This list is a SMALL SUBSET of upstream's
         116 extensions (11 here); it is NOT a full port and does not claim
         parity.

  rules/*.md
      Original prose written for this project. NOT derived from open-code-review
      and NOT expert-validated: every document carries
      `needs-expert-review: true`.

Everything else in this directory — the bundle-cost join, the review order, the
rule library, `render_scope`, the fixtures and the test suite — is original to
this project.

